<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Zhex is a Forth-inspired language built on small words for big ideas.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f3ec">
  <title>Zhex — Small words. Big ideas.</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="./" aria-label="Zhex home"><img class="brand-logo" src="logo.svg" width="168" height="50" alt=""></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="examples.html">Examples</a>
      <a href="#start">Get started</a>
      <a href="roadmap.html">Roadmap</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/desireco/zhex">GitHub ↗</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">A Forth-inspired language</p>
        <h1>Small words.<br><span class="accent-line">Big ideas.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Compact code with visible flow, meaningful names, and checked types.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="examples.html">Read the examples <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#start">Try Zhex locally ↓</a>
        </div>
        <p class="status"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Experimental · Working Go interpreter</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="code-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">One file · One flow</p><h2 id="code-title">See where every value goes.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">Read a name, pass it through one word, and print the result. The program stays compact without hiding its sequence.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="code-window">
        <div class="code-window__head"><a href="examples.html#hello">hello.zhex →</a><span>Console input → output</span></div>
        <pre><code>{{.HeroSource | highlight}}</code></pre>
        <div class="console"><span>With input: {{.HeroInput}}</span>{{.HeroOutput}}</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section principles-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Readable foundations</p><h2 id="principles-title">Compact does not have to mean cryptic.</h2></div>
          <p class="intro">Zhex keeps the compositional spirit of Forth while making data movement and intent easier to follow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principles">
          <article class="principle"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Flow</p><h3>Visible movement.</h3><p>Explicit flows show how one result becomes the next input.</p></article>
          <article class="principle"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Meaning</p><h3>Named values.</h3><p>Important values carry names instead of living only as stack positions.</p></article>
          <article class="principle"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Confidence</p><h3>Checked types.</h3><p>Word signatures catch mismatches before a program reaches its result.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Start with code</p><h2 id="examples-title">Four programs. Four practical ideas.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">Follow the language from console input through conditions, loops, local state, and text operations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <a class="feature-row" href="examples.html#hello"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Hello, console.</h3><p>Read a name and print a greeting.</p></a>
        <a class="feature-row" href="examples.html#fizzbuzz"><span class="number">02</span><h3>FizzBuzz</h3><p>Combine conditions, loops, and output.</p></a>
        <a class="feature-row" href="examples.html#fibonacci"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Fibonacci</h3><p>Calculate a result with local state.</p></a>
        <a class="feature-row" href="examples.html#palindrome"><span class="number">04</span><h3>Palindrome</h3><p>Read text and check its reverse.</p></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section start-section" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Run it yourself</p><h2 id="start-title">Run your first Zhex program.</h2></div>
          <p class="intro">Build and run with Go 1.23 or newer. The interpreter supports small working programs today; repository access is required for local setup.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="command-block"><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/desireco/zhex.git
cd zhex
go run ./cmd/zhex run examples/hello.zhex</code></pre></div>
        <p class="access-note">The source repository is currently private. You can still <a href="examples.html">browse and download the public examples</a> or <a href="roadmap.html">review what comes next</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="./" aria-label="Zhex home"><img class="brand-logo" src="logo.svg" width="138" height="41" alt=""></a>
    <p>Small words. Big ideas.</p>
    <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Footer navigation">
